CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20 --object-bits 11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ constexpr decltype\(auto\) get chain: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.spec.auto] + [temp.point]/1 + [temp.inst]/5: a constexpr function
template with a deduced (decltype(auto)) return type forwarding to a constexpr
function template with a derived-to-base pack parameter (the std::get ->
__get_helper -> _Tuple_impl::_M_head shape).

A constexpr specialization reached for a run-time call is deferred to the clean
method-body drain so its derived-to-base pack call resolves -- but one whose
return type must be deduced (auto/decltype(auto)) must still be converted
eagerly so the return type is known before its call sites.  Deferring the
auto-return wrapper would leave it unbindable; eagerly converting the non-auto
inner function would drop its derived-to-base pack call.  Assertion 2 (a wrong
value) FAILs, proving non-vacuity.
